<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  StochCraft's vendor extensions to BPSim 2.0 and 1.0 (MIT OR Apache-2.0).

  BPSim's VendorExtension takes a `name` and, for its value, attributes and elements from another
  namespace, which a validator checks strictly: this schema declares StochCraft's. Validate with
  it imported next to the BPSim schema.

    <bpsim:VendorExtension name="stochcraft:queueCapacity"
        xmlns:stochcraft="https://helenkwok.github.io/StochCraft/bpsim/1" stochcraft:value="3"/>

  stochcraft:queueCapacity, on a task's ElementParameters: the most entities that wait for the
  task's resource (not counting those in service), a whole number of at least 0.

  stochcraft:pool, on a resource's ElementParameters, with the value true: the resource is a
  shared pool, even when one task uses it or none. Without it, a resource that one task needs a
  single unit of may be read as that task's own resource.

  stochcraft:batchSize, on a task's ElementParameters: the task collects this many entities
  (a whole number of at least 1) and sends them on together as one batch.

  stochcraft:unbatch, on a task's ElementParameters, with the value true: the task splits each
  batch back into its entities.

  stochcraft:quantity, on the ElementParameters of a sequence flow into a parallel gateway: how
  many entities from that flow go into each one the gateway sends on (a bill of materials;
  a whole number of at least 1).

  stochcraft:breakdown, on a task's ElementParameters: its resource's units fail after a time
  drawn from timeToFailure (elapsed since the last repair) and are repaired for a time drawn from
  repairTime, each holding one BPSim distribution or constant. Whether a failure interrupts the
  job under way is BPSim's own PriorityParameters/Interruptible. With handsOnWhileDown="false", a
  unit that fails while holding a finished part keeps it until repaired (by default it hands it
  on as soon as there is room).

    <bpsim:VendorExtension name="stochcraft:breakdown" xmlns:stochcraft="…">
      <stochcraft:breakdown>
        <stochcraft:timeToFailure><bpsim:ExponentialDistribution mean="480"/></stochcraft:timeToFailure>
        <stochcraft:repairTime><bpsim:TriangularDistribution min="10" mode="20" max="60"/></stochcraft:repairTime>
      </stochcraft:breakdown>
    </bpsim:VendorExtension>

  stochcraft:transferTime, on a task's ElementParameters: the time a part takes to reach the
  task from the element that sends it, holding one BPSim distribution or constant. The part
  takes its place in the task's buffer (queueCapacity) when the transfer starts and joins the
  queue when it ends; a sending task's resource stays occupied through the transfer, unless the
  attribute holdsSender is false: then it is free at once, and the time is a minimum time in the
  buffer.

    <bpsim:VendorExtension name="stochcraft:transferTime" xmlns:stochcraft="…">
      <stochcraft:transferTime holdsSender="false"><bpsim:FloatingParameter value="32"/></stochcraft:transferTime>
    </bpsim:VendorExtension>

  stochcraft:plannedRunTime, on a task's ElementParameters: the planned time for the task's
  resource to make one item (ISO 22400-2's planned runtime per item), holding one BPSim
  distribution or constant whose mean is the plan. It is not simulated; results use it for
  effectiveness and OEE.

    <bpsim:VendorExtension name="stochcraft:plannedRunTime" xmlns:stochcraft="…">
      <stochcraft:plannedRunTime><bpsim:FloatingParameter value="30"/></stochcraft:plannedRunTime>
    </bpsim:VendorExtension>

  stochcraft:changeover, on a task's ElementParameters: its resource's unit sets up before a part
  only when the part's value of the token property named by the attribute property differs from
  that of the part the unit served last (its first part needs none). The setup takes the time of
  the stochcraft:change whose from and to are the two values, else stochcraft:time, each holding
  one BPSim distribution or constant. A setup before every job is BPSim's own
  TimeParameters/SetUpTime.

    <bpsim:VendorExtension name="stochcraft:changeover" xmlns:stochcraft="…">
      <stochcraft:changeover property="type">
        <stochcraft:time><bpsim:FloatingParameter value="10"/></stochcraft:time>
        <stochcraft:change from="A" to="B"><bpsim:FloatingParameter value="25"/></stochcraft:change>
      </stochcraft:changeover>
    </bpsim:VendorExtension>

  stochcraft:routing, on an exclusive gateway's ElementParameters, with the value shortestQueue
  (or standard, BPMN's own routing): each entity goes to the way with the fewest entities waiting
  or in transit among those with room, a tie to the way taken longest ago; while no way has
  room, the element sending into the gateway waits (a task's resource stays blocked) and a
  start event's arrival is lost.

  stochcraft:power, on a task's ElementParameters: the power each unit of the task's resource
  draws in each state, in kilowatts (numbers of at least 0): processing and idle (both needed),
  and blocked, failed and offShift, each idle when left out.

    <bpsim:VendorExtension name="stochcraft:power" xmlns:stochcraft="…">
      <stochcraft:power processing="12.5" idle="2" failed="0.5" offShift="0"/>
    </bpsim:VendorExtension>

  stochcraft:stopCount, on an element's ElementParameters: each replication ends once this many
  entities (a whole number of at least 1) have left the element since time 0 (for an end event:
  arrived there), or at the scenario's duration if that comes first.

  stochcraft:stopWhenEmpty, on a task's ElementParameters, with the value true: each replication
  ends the first time the task holds no entity, none waiting and none in service, after it has
  taken one in.

  stochcraft:estimate, on the ElementParameters of an element with a time distribution (a start
  event's interTriggerTimer, a task's processingTime): the three-point estimate the distribution
  was fitted from, kept as its pedigree. The distribution itself is the standard BPSim one in the
  parameters; this records where it came from. Exactly one of max and p95.

    <bpsim:VendorExtension name="stochcraft:estimate" xmlns:stochcraft="…">
      <stochcraft:estimate family="pert" min="10" mode="20" max="60" source="Delphi, round 2"/>
    </bpsim:VendorExtension>
-->
<xs:schema xmlns:xs="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema"
    xmlns:stochcraft="https://helenkwok.github.io/StochCraft/bpsim/1"
    targetNamespace="https://helenkwok.github.io/StochCraft/bpsim/1"
    elementFormDefault="qualified">
  <xs:attribute name="value" type="xs:string"/>
  <xs:complexType name="Value">
    <xs:sequence>
      <xs:any namespace="http://www.bpsim.org/schemas/2.0 http://www.bpsim.org/schemas/1.0"
          processContents="lax"/>
    </xs:sequence>
  </xs:complexType>
  <xs:element name="breakdown">
    <xs:complexType>
      <xs:sequence>
        <xs:element name="timeToFailure" type="stochcraft:Value"/>
        <xs:element name="repairTime" type="stochcraft:Value"/>
      </xs:sequence>
      <xs:attribute name="handsOnWhileDown" type="xs:boolean" default="true"/>
    </xs:complexType>
  </xs:element>
  <xs:element name="transferTime">
    <xs:complexType>
      <xs:complexContent>
        <xs:extension base="stochcraft:Value">
          <xs:attribute name="holdsSender" type="xs:boolean" default="true"/>
        </xs:extension>
      </xs:complexContent>
    </xs:complexType>
  </xs:element>
  <xs:element name="plannedRunTime" type="stochcraft:Value"/>
  <xs:element name="changeover">
    <xs:complexType>
      <xs:sequence>
        <xs:element name="time" type="stochcraft:Value"/>
        <xs:element name="change" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
          <xs:complexType>
            <xs:complexContent>
              <xs:extension base="stochcraft:Value">
                <xs:attribute name="from" type="xs:string" use="required"/>
                <xs:attribute name="to" type="xs:string" use="required"/>
              </xs:extension>
            </xs:complexContent>
          </xs:complexType>
        </xs:element>
      </xs:sequence>
      <xs:attribute name="property" type="xs:string" use="required"/>
    </xs:complexType>
  </xs:element>
  <xs:element name="power">
    <xs:complexType>
      <xs:attribute name="processing" type="xs:double" use="required"/>
      <xs:attribute name="idle" type="xs:double" use="required"/>
      <xs:attribute name="blocked" type="xs:double"/>
      <xs:attribute name="failed" type="xs:double"/>
      <xs:attribute name="offShift" type="xs:double"/>
    </xs:complexType>
  </xs:element>
  <xs:element name="estimate">
    <xs:complexType>
      <xs:attribute name="family" use="required">
        <xs:simpleType>
          <xs:restriction base="xs:string">
            <xs:enumeration value="triangular"/>
            <xs:enumeration value="pert"/>
            <xs:enumeration value="lognormal"/>
            <xs:enumeration value="weibull"/>
          </xs:restriction>
        </xs:simpleType>
      </xs:attribute>
      <xs:attribute name="min" type="xs:double" use="required"/>
      <xs:attribute name="mode" type="xs:double" use="required"/>
      <xs:attribute name="max" type="xs:double"/>
      <xs:attribute name="p95" type="xs:double"/>
      <xs:attribute name="source" type="xs:string"/>
    </xs:complexType>
  </xs:element>
</xs:schema>
